ceived_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #2108 (fixture follow-up only; excludes #1961 dependency qualification and #2106 integration).\n\n**Cause.** `scripts/isolated_rust_tests.py` sets `TMPDIR=<per-user temp>/corbanu-tests-XXXX/tmp` (75 bytes on this Mac). `TempDir::new()` + `.tmpXXXXXX/app-server-control/app-server-control.sock` then exceeds macOS `sun_path` (104 incl. NUL), so `start_control_socket_acceptor` returns `InvalidInput: path must be shorter than SUN_LEN`.\n\n**Change (test code only).** `socket_test_dir()` keeps the usual self-removing `TempDir` under TMPDIR and falls back to a randomly named **0700** directory under `/tmp` only when the socket path would not fit (103 bytes macOS/BSD, 107 Linux). The two socket tests use it. Unchanged: the 0600 socket assertion, the WebSocket upgrade/text/ping assertions, the startup-lock fixtures, the disposable profile and keyring denial, and every production socket path and permission.\n\nNew test `socket_test_dir_fits_sun_path_and_stays_private_under_a_long_temp_root`: a 120-byte root forces the fallback; it checks the path fits, the mode is 0700, two fixtures never share a directory, and the directory is removed on drop. (Its first run caught that tempfile creates 0755 under the default umask, so the fallback sets 0700 explicitly.)\n\n**Evidence (macOS 26, aarch64).** cargo-nextest is not installed here, so the replay imports the wrapper's own `test_environment()` and rebuilds its profile/TMPDIR layout, then runs `cargo test -p codex-app-server-transport --lib --locked --offline`:\n- base: 150 passed, 2 failed (both SUN_LEN), exit 101\n- head: 153 passed, exit 0\n- control with the default TMPDIR: 153 passed, exit 0\n- clippy `--tests -D warnings`: 0; fmt `--check`: 0\n\nNot run: Linux and Windows (CI covers them). On Windows the fixture is unchanged.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reas